# ─── Data exports (PII) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.csv

# Narrow exceptions: two GENERATED contract inventories, deliberately tracked.
#
# Both are route/endpoint ledgers — HTTP method, path, route name, handler
# class, and the source file each was found in. Neither contains member data,
# so the PII reason for the blanket rule above does not apply. They are named
# individually rather than by a directory or `*matrix.csv` glob, so the rule
# keeps catching every genuine data export.
#
# They were silently lost in the 2026-08-09 repository move: the tooling and
# docs still referred to them (aspnet-backend/docs/generated/
# canonical-react-contracts/README.md calls the first one "the complete
# deduplicated matrix"), but the blanket rule above meant neither was ever
# staged, so only their .json/.md siblings survived. Regenerate with
# `npm --prefix web-uk run route:matrix` and
# `aspnet-backend/scripts/generate-canonical-react-contract-matrix.ps1`.
!aspnet-backend/docs/generated/canonical-react-contracts/canonical-react-api-contract-matrix.csv
!web-uk/docs/generated/accessible-route-matrix.csv

# ─── Legacy analysis / scratch artifacts (cleanup 2026-04-13) ────────────────
